At this point in the update, the  machine has loaded the new firmware
into memory.  At the point where it stops, it is trying to boot from
the firmware image in memory.

Perhaps in a previous life this machine had its console set to serial
on the SRM side.  Try plugging in a terminal at 9600,8n1 on the lowest
numbered serial port.   You may see some output.

 > Now, the documentation for the fail safe booting indicates I should
